speechtext:
Then I understand there is no discussion on item 82. We will proceed to item 134.
Customs tariff-134. All sugar above No. 16 Dutch standard in colour, and all refined sugars of whatever kinds, grades or standards, not covered by tariff item No. 135, when not exceeding eighty-eight degrees of polarization, per one hundred pounds: British preferential tariff, 83 cents; most favoured nation tariff, $1.50; general tariff $1.50;
When exceeding eighty-eight degrees but not exceeding eighty-nine degrees, per one hundred pounds: British preferential tariff, 85 cents; most favoured nation tariff, $1.53; general tariff, $1.53;
When exceeding eighty-nine degrees but not exceeding ninety degrees, per one hundred pounds: British preferential tariff, 87 cents; most favoured nation tariff, $1.55; general tariff, $1.55;
When exceeding ninety degrees but not exceeding ninety one degrees, per one hundred pounds: British preferential tariff, 89 cents; most favoured nation tariff, $1.58; general tariff, $1.58;
When exceeding ninety one degrees but not exceeding ninety two degrees, per one hundred pounds: British preferential tariff, 91 cents; most favoured nation tariff, $1.62; general tariff, $1.62;
When exceeding ninety two degrees but not exceeding ninety three degrees, per one hundred pounds: British preferential tariff, 93 cents; most favoured nation tariff, $1.65; general tariff, $1.65;
When exceeding ninety three degrees but not exceeding ninety four degrees, per one hundred pounds: British preferential tariff, 95 cents; most favoured nation tariff, $1.68; general tariff, $1.68;
When exceeding ninety four degrees but not exceeding ninety five degrees, per one hundred pounds: British preferential tariff, 97 cents; most favoured nation tariff, $1.70; general tariff, $1.70;
When exceeding ninety five degrees but not exceeding ninety six degrees, per one hundred pounds: British preferential tariff, 99 cents; most favoured nation tariff, $1.74; general tariff, $1.74;
When exceeding ninety six degrees but not exceeding ninety seven degrees, per one hundred pounds:	British preferential tariff, $1.01; most
favoured nation tariff, $1.77; general tariff, $1.77;
When exceeding ninety seven degrees but not exceeding ninety eight degrees, per one hundred pounds:	British preferential tariff, $1.03; most
favoured nation tariff, $1.80; general tariff, $1.80;

Customs Tariff
When exceeding ninety eight degrees, but not exceeding ninety nine degrees, per one hundred pounds:	British preferential tariff, $1.09; most
favoured nation tariff, $1.89; general tariff, $1.89;
When exceeding ninety nine degrees, per one hundred pounds: British preferential tariff, $1.09; most favoured nation tariff, $1.89; general tariff, $1.89;
Refined sugar shall be entitled to entry under the British preferential tariff upon evidence satisfactory to the minister that such refined sugar has been manufactured wholly from raw sugar produced in the British colonies and possessions, and not otherwise.
Sugar imported under this item shall not be subject to special duty in excess of three-fourths of one cent per pound.

I move:
That resolution No. 1 of the budget resolutions relating to the customs tariff be amended to provide for the further amendment to schedule A by striking out tariff item 137, the enumeration of goods and the rate of duty of customs set opposite the said item and by inserting the following item, enumeration and rates of duties in the said schedule A:
137. Molasses, produced by the evaporation and partial inversion of the juice of the sugar cane, in which the percentage of sulphated ash is not more than 9 per cent by weight, for human consumption only, per gallon: British preferential tariff, free; most favoured nation tariff, 1 cent; general tariff, 11 cents;

Then I understand we have now reached item 140.
Customs tariff-140. Syrups, the product of the sugar cane or beet, and all imitations thereof or substitutes therefor, n.o.p. per gallon:	British
preferential tariff, 5 cents; most favoured nation tariff, 6j| cents; general tariff, 7 cents;

Item agreed to.
Customs tariff-157a. Amyl alcohol:	British
preferential tariff, free; most favoured nation tariff, free; general tariff, free;

Item agreed to.
Customs tariff-438c. Ammeters; arm rests and wheel housing lining of indurated fibre, pressed to shape; axle housings, one piece welded, machined or not, including parts welded thereto; carburetors; chassis frames and steel shapes for the manufacture thereof; cigar and cigarette lighters, whether in combination with a cigarette holder or not, including base; control ventilator gear box; cylinder lock barrels, with or without sleeves and keys thereof; dash heat indicators; engine speed governor units; external ornaments unplated, including name plates, letter and numerals, but not including finish or decorative mouldings; fluid couplings with or without drive plate assemblies; gauges, gasoline, oil or air;
Grilles not plated, polished or not before assembly, and parts thereof not plated or polished after final forming, casting or piercing, not including added finish or decorative mouldings; hinges, finished or not, for bodies; horns; instrument bezel assemblies; instrument board lamps; instrument panel, glove compartment, luggage compartment, hood compartment and door step lamps and wire assemblies; locks, electric ignition, steering gear, transmission, or combinations of such locks; mouldings of metal, with nails set in position, lead filled or not; oil filter parts, namely: perforated filter refill oil board bodies, refill end discs, and roll-seam perforated tubes; ornaments and identification plates of metal, unplated, not including finished or decorative mouldings;
